--[[ HubNPCData (ModuleScript) -> ReplicatedStorage/Spellshot/HubNPCData
	GENERATED by hub/hub_life_2026_10_25/npcs/export_hubnpc.py from keeper.blend + merchant.blend and (2026-10-27)
	the seven ambient NPCs' .blends (built by npcs/build_npc.py from design_<key>.py) -- do not edit by hand.

	Nine hub NPCs, all the R15 HubLifeMannequin wearing rigid accessory meshes, plus free props, plus authored
	Blender clips baked to Motor6D.Transform per frame:
	  Keeper (Loadout Keeper / Terra) and Merchant (Shop Merchant / Pyro): Idle + Greet, a prompt, a look-at.
	  (2026-10-27) Ambient = true: ONE looping Idle each and nothing else (no Greet, no prompt, no look-at, nothing
	  reacting to players): TrainingDrill (palm thrusts down target T_a's lane), TrainingWatch (left shoulder on the
	  Training entrance pillar), DuelsWatchA / DuelsWatchB (arms folded on the Duels terrace step), StoreTalk /
	  StoreListen (a pair chatting by the stair's featured-item display), StoreLean (back and right sole on the stair wall).
	Accessory + prop triangles: Keeper 1910, Merchant 2042, TrainingDrill 518, TrainingWatch 778, DuelsWatchA 848, DuelsWatchB 812, StoreTalk 878, StoreListen 886, StoreLean 890.

	Conventions
	- Roblox axes, studs. Each NPC's local space = its HumanoidRootPart (HRP) at the origin, facing -Z.
	- All numbers are comma-joined integers in strings. Positions = thousandths of a stud.
	  Quaternions = (w, x, y, z) in thousandths: divide by 1000 and RENORMALISE before CFrame.new(x,y,z,qx,qy,qz,qw).
	- Rest pose = the Motor6D rest (Transform = identity): Part1 = Part0 * C0 * C1:Inverse(), C0/C1 exactly as
	  in rig/r15_mannequin.json (the JSON part 'Pos' values are not used). Floor = y -3.192 (HRP centre 3.192 above
	  the floor = HipHeight 2.192 + 1; the rest pose's foot bottoms sit exactly there). The Keeper's hem stays above it.
	- Pieces: V = unique vertices x,y,z in the LOCAL space of the ride part's rest CFrame (or of the prop for
	  Ride = "Prop:<Name>"); T = triangles, 0-based vertex indices, counter-clockwise seen from outside (front
	  faces). Shading is meant to be flat (faceted): split vertices per triangle or use face normals.
	- Body: Color for every R15 part; Hide = parts fully covered by pieces (make them Transparency 1).
	- Props.<Name>.Rest = px,py,pz,qw,qx,qy,qz: the prop CFrame relative to the HRP before any clip plays.
	- Lights: At = x,y,z (thousandths) in the ride's local space; effective Brightness = Brightness * glow.
	- Clips: Fps 30, N frames. Joints.<Motor6D name> = N x (qw,qx,qy,qz,px,py,pz): the Motor6D.Transform per
	  frame (joints that never move are omitted = identity). Root motion is in Root's Transform; the HRP never moves.
	  Props.<Name> = N x (px,py,pz,qw,qx,qy,qz) relative to the HRP. Glow.<Channel> = N x 0..1000 (0..1), driving
	  Neon classes with Glow = <Channel> and Lights with Glow = <Channel>.
	  Idle loops (frame N would equal frame 0). Greet is one-shot; it starts and ends on Idle frame 0;
	  PromptAt = seconds into Greet when the acknowledgement lands (show the prompt then).
	  Keeper / Merchant: no Neck yaw is baked: add the look-at yaw on the Neck on top of the clip.
	  (2026-10-27) Ambient NPCs: their Neck yaw IS baked (head pans, eyes on the target, glances): add NOTHING on
	  the Neck. Their joints are keyed every 1-3 frames so the planted feet, contacts and props hold on every frame;
	  any joint's Transform may carry a position (the Store pair's shoulder shrug, StoreLean's Neck -0.03 z).
	- (2026-10-27) Ambient contact, HRP space: every ambient NPC's boot soles stand on y -3.192 (DuelsWatchA/B on the
	  Duels terrace step, StoreLean on the trough ridge at the stair wall's foot). TrainingWatch's pillar face is the
	  plane x = -0.95 (normal +X, his left shoulder cap flush on it); his body stands about +1.45 X of the HRP (feet
	  at x 1.2..2.3). StoreLean's wall is the plane z = +0.75 (behind him, normal -Z): his back and his right boot
	  sole lie flat on it. Glow channels with no Neon class (the cape / sash-tail / satchel props) are harmless.
	- Merchant: Root carries a constant lift (+0.62) and shift toward the counter (-0.56 z): he stands on an implied
	  0.62-stud step behind the counter so his forearms rest on the top at y = +0.494. His legs are below the
	  counter top; his feet float 0.62 above the floor if the back of the counter is ever visible (add a step).
]]
